[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "caro-classical-ng5 5...e6"]
[Name "Classical: 5.Ng5 e6 6.Bd3"]

6. Bd3 { Cuts the queen off from d4. [%csl Rd4] }
6... Qxd4 { Black wins a pawn. The bishop on f5 is guarded, so nothing hangs. [%idea blocked-guard] }
7. N1f3
( 7. Be3? { Hits the queen, but it blocks nothing and leaves the king in the centre. }
  7... Bb4+ 8. Ke2 Bxd3+ 9. Qxd3 Qxd3+ 10. cxd3 { The queens are off, White's king has lost the right to castle and the pawns are doubled, and Black is a clean pawn up. } )
7... Qd5 { Stands safely in the middle of the board: if the bishops come off on f5, so do the queens, and Black keeps the pawn. } *
